So you want a really buff marilith? The only ways to level a pet
beyond its natural threshold are feeding it wraith corpses or giving
it potions of gain level to quaff. Since mariliths are non-eating
pets, you will need to give it potions of gain level. However, since
your pet was freshly polymorphed, it isn't close to its EXP threshold
yet. Give it some wimpy monsters to kill, checking by stethescope or
wand of probing to determine when it hits the threshold, *then* let it
quaff.

As for keeping it alive, either keep it by your side at all times, or
genocide t and w. Even an archon or arch-lich with 400 HP can't
survive the digestive system of a purple worm. And keep demonic pets
away from blue jellies for obvious reasons.

Then, you mentioned rings and amulets. I'm not an expert, but I
*think* monsters only wear amulets of life saving, not reflection. If
you want her (Mariliths look like six-armed snake ladies) to have
reflection, I believe your marilith will don a shield of reflection.

If all fails and your pet croaks, turns to slime, etc., then keep in
mind that Mariliths are the easiest demonic pet to acquire provided
you have polymorph control. If you poly into a marilith, then every so
often you'll get the message "some hell-p has arrived" and acquire a
tame marilith.

Last but not least, zapping your pet with a wand of polymorph is
dangerous because there's a 1/25 chance per zap of a system shock
destroying your pet. Next time, maybe zap Fido once or twice, but save
a few charges for the wand of polymorph's true function: polypiling.
For a wizard (I assume you played a wizard if you started with a wand
of polymorph), you can safely polymorph your blessed spellbook of
force bolt several times to greatly expand your starting spell
repertoire. It's risky because you won't *keep* the spellbooks you
read, but you can rewrite the important ones with a magic marker with
100% success. Other uses include zapping at elven boots/cloaks (which
count as magical armor) to get magical armor such as speed boots and
gauntlets of power.



